cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyuncho (동현초): an educational Drosophila brain-circuit laboratory controlled through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "1.22"
date-released: "2026-10-26"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23689484"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab1"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab1/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyuncho is a browser-based, noncommercial educational laboratory in
  which a cartoon fruit fly is driven by 1,758 neurons and 121,135 directed
  connections selected from the FlyWire v783 adult Drosophila brain
  connectome, computed with an adapted version of the Shiu et al. (2024)
  brain model. Stimuli and readouts are specified only through the esoteric
  programming language Donghyun-lang. It is a teaching tool, not a
  whole-brain model or a biological measurement. The MIT license applies only
  to the original application code and documentation; the FlyWire data are
  distributed under the noncommercial FlyWire guidance (CC BY-NC 4.0), and
  the fonts under the SIL Open Font License. See LICENSE, CREDITS.md and
  PROVENANCE.md.
keywords:
  - neuroscience education
  - Drosophila
  - connectome
  - FlyWire
  - computational neuroscience
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
